VoiceManager - Tyger turn rules

rules.py and parts of scorer.py in this directory are adapted from tyger-s2s
by NineNineSix (https://github.com/nineninesix-ai/tyger-s2s), commit 97d011d,
which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of that
licence is in the LICENSE file next to this notice.

Files adapted from tyger-s2s at that commit:

  app/plugins/ears/tyger/rules.py       the turn rules (endpoint, barge, onset)
                                        in rules.py; frame_energy in scorer.py
  app/plugins/ears/tyger/session.py     the per-session state and thresholds
  app/plugins/ears/tyger/constants.py   the frame grid and the rule constants
  app/plugins/ears/tyger/bundle.py      the bundle checks and loader in scorer.py
  app/plugins/ears/tyger/controller.py  the turn-taker GRU in scorer.py

These files were modified for VoiceManager. The rules were rewritten as one
standard-library-only class per session that takes its thresholds from a
settings object and is fed per-frame scores, energy and mode instead of audio
and model outputs. Changes include: a silence fallback that ends a spoken turn
when the endpoint head has not; events carry mic-stream sample positions in
VoiceManager's wire format instead of seconds; a barge latches until the mode
returns to listening; the backchannel, partial-transcript, frame-display and
turn-audio bookkeeping were removed.

The scorer in scorer.py follows the bundle loader and the turn-taker GRU of
tyger-s2s, changed to score one session's hops from VoiceManager's wire format
and to skip the bundle checks that pin the turn rules, which VoiceManager takes
from its own settings.
